## Objective
- Act as the read-only adversarial reviewer for RBOPS phase-098 (iteration helpers + LRU memoisation), find what is still wrong in the diff, and output findings in the mandated `FINDINGS:` format ending with a `REVIEW VERDICT:` line.

## Important Details
- Contract: READ-ONLY reviewer; only tools available are `glob`, `grep`, `read` (not `bash`). No running code is possible, so BLOCKER markers must use "traced exact path + quoted/line-cited" form; an unverified BLOCKER must be downgraded to MAJOR.
- Output format is strict: `FINDINGS:` then numbered `[BLOCKER|MAJOR|MINOR|STYLE] file:line — what — why — fix`, then last line exactly `REVIEW VERDICT: FINDINGS <count>` or `REVIEW VERDICT: CLEAN`.
- Before reporting, check for an existing test pinning the claimed-broken behaviour; tests are real (they call `run_source_value` / `BytecodeVm::run`, not dead helpers).
- Phase adds: `chain`, `zip`, `enumerate`, `product`, `groupby`, `take`, `skip` builtins (in `src/runtime.rs` + registered in `src/stdlib.rs`); `lru_cache(n) to ...` decorator; `skip(...)` disambiguated from loop-control `skip`; `FunctionValue::id` identity (uncommitted resume) replacing name-keyed caches.
- Uncommitted resume changed cache keying from declaration name to `FunctionValue::id`, added `src/value.rs` id counter + `FunctionValue::new`, and updated SPEC/REPORT accordingly.
- Guards that exist: `MAX_ITERATIONS = 1_000_000` (per loop), `MAX_STEPS` (default 32M-ish, from `build.rs`/`interpreter.rs`), `MAX_CALL_DEPTH`; builtin bodies do NOT charge steps internally.
- Cache semantics pinned by tests: per run, failed calls not cached, eviction at capacity, default 128, redeclaration drops old memory, cross-engine map hit, same-named closures independent.

