### Active
- Drafting findings. Candidate findings established so far:
  1. **BLOCKER (traced)** `src/bytecode/vm.rs` ~3196 + `advance_map` ~3154: a cache hit inside `map` calls `advance_map`, which calls `call_function`, which on another hit calls `advance_map` again — one Rust stack frame per consecutive cache hit. Map over ~tens of thousands of equal already-cached values overflows the process stack (abort, not `Error::Limit`); no call-depth charge on hits (explicit comment). Reachable: build a large list of the same value in a loop (≤1M iterations) then `map(xs, cached_fn)`.
  2. **MAJOR** `src/interpreter.rs` ~2253-2263: `replaced` only looks at `self.locals.last()`, but each loop iteration pushes a fresh scope (`run_iteration_body` ~1064-1065), so a decorated declaration written directly in a loop body never finds the previous binding and registers a new `id` cache every iteration — caches grow unbounded per turn. Contradicts the code comment and REPORT claim ("keeps a cached declaration in a loop from accumulating unreachable caches"). VM does not leak in this shape (same frame/globals), so cross-engine resource divergence.
  3. **MAJOR** `src/runtime.rs` product (~1698) `Vec::with_capacity(left.len().saturating_mul(right.len()))`: two easily-built 100k lists → 1e10 entries → allocation failure aborts; bypasses step budget (builtin costs one step). Also `groupby` is O(n²) with Value equality (~1725+), 1M distinct keys ≈ 5e11 comparisons, no step charge/timeout — a single call can hang past the step limit.
  4. **MAJOR (optional/lower confidence)** `src/bytecode/vm.rs` ~2910 hidden declare uses `self.get_var(declared)` (locals-first, `get_var` ~1410) while a file-module frame binds via `globals_only` (`bind` ~2317) — an importing scope's local of the same name shadows the just-stored module function, so cache registers on the wrong id or import fails with `lru_cache declaration '<name>' is not a function`, diverging from the tree-walker. Root cause (module frames reading outer locals) may be pre-existing.
  5. **MAJOR / design-vs-SPEC** cache side table keyed by `id` is never removed when a closure becomes unreachable (factory loop `set f to make(i)`): memory does not "belong to the function value" as SPEC now says; pre-resume name keying overwrote and was bounded.
- Formatter prints `lru_cache(128)` for the omitted-capacity spelling (parser default); idempotent, not reported.
- Tests lack any large-list/map-cache stress test and any module-decorated-function test.

### Blocked
- Cannot run `cargo test`/repro; all BLOCKER verification must be trace-based with quoted lines.

